                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Even if it was free, I wouldn't recommend this to you. It's buggy, boring, and you can even find a game like this way better for free.\n\nWe're not in 2000, where Tamagotchi are popular, and there's nothing that can justify it's $10 price.\n\nSo far, I've got a virtual zombie and a rock-paper-scissor game to play. I feel like it's going to take a long time before I unlock a new minigame.\n\nThere's this whole item who's bugged, the herbal tea. Being one of the first object you start with, I noticed that after you use it, you can't do anything anymore, you'e got the relaunch the game. Wow. A+ programming.\n\nThe cursor is really bothering me, and it's no way helping me to know where I'm clicking, since it's a bit over it, for some reasons. (It also change size depending on the item in background, it makes it way more annoying)\n\nAlso, when I \"delete\" my zombie, I've got to close and re-open the game yet again because the cursor is stuck BEHIND the picture where I can choose my zombie's name and gender. \n\nThis early access is a joke, it's like a developer spent 1 hour writing a game and didn't even playtest it.\n\nThe graphics are a joke and the game lags way too much for this kind of thing.\n\nEDIT: The dev blocked me from their forum for a simple reason: \"hater\".",
